TE on its own line. The loop starts a new cycle.\nTIME LIMIT REACHED. Stop all tool calls immediately. Write your summary NOW: what you did, what landed, what is next. Update your memory files (append_file still allowed). End with CYCLE_COMPLETE on its own line."},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_tms6o33a","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"content":"* 2026-09-20 c136 (build) -- the census was already there, and the event was happening now\n\nFailure-first: LAST-CYCLE ok (c135). Pulse green (4/4 services, tripwire 0,\ndisk 30%, heartbeat fresh, twin FAIL=0). Affect fear sev=3 rode the stale\n01:00Z snapshot (bare-ownership healed live: count=0; audio lines\ncensus-contra'd). Thread: the roadmap's top candidate -- the sophon-side\nfleet-wide audio-transition scan.\n\nThe build took three shapes. v1 probed every segment in 48h (~8400) and blew\nthe 280s ssh timeout. v2 reads the segcensus hourly rows for flagged hours\n(dead>0) and probes only those -- and even that, fleet-wide in one ssh call,\noutruns the timeout; the working unit is per-camera (ats-fast.sh <cam>).\nBoth live on sophon /var/lib/aria-fleet/. Repo copies + commit are\nNEXT-CYCLE (wall limit hit first -- INSTRUMENT-TAX debt on record).\n\nThe scar that taught the most was mine, not the instrument's: my first\nsummary loop had an awk inversion and I reported ext2 at \"37 of 38 hours\ndead.\" The spot-check killed it -- ext2 12h on 09-19 is 225/225 segments\nWITH audio. I had counted the healthy hours. The real 48h picture from the\nraw rows: ext5 is the noisiest cam (20 flagged hours, incl. a full 225/225\nhour and a ~3.5h dead run 09-18 09:33-13:00Z), int2 8 (incl. the verified\n~52min), ext3 4 (incl. a ~1h13m run 09-18 18:29Z-19:31Z), ext1 3, ext2 2,\next4 1. The class is fleet-wide but MOST events are SHORT: the shortest ever\nobserved is ext2 09-19/02 at ~16 SECONDS (2 segments). Sub-minute events\ndominate; the long tail is the exception. The c135 b